sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4, 5 (swamp role SSH identity), round 2 bugs (server admin password by its own vault key), flow-tighten (rules 6, 22: no ownership probe or fence, scripts in argv). docs/reference/database-servers.md#remove-a-database.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: database:destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>beast-mysql server
  CLI->>GW: database:destroy shop<br/>--force
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit database:destroy shop --force`
  %%> - syntax: `<slug> [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the connection slug, as `database:list` shows it
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--force`, the CLI asks first; the default is No
  %%> - with `--json` or without a terminal, `--force` is required (`database.confirmation_required`)
  Note over GW: Check, plan the removal<br/>task #5124 · lock beast-mysql
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - no Instance attaches `shop` (`database.connection_attached`); detach with `instance:database:remove` first
  %%> - AI router setup and Analytics do not use it
  %%> - no database creation or other removal runs on `beast-mysql`; the Gateway holds one lock per Database server
  %%> Plans:
  %%> - the databases: `shop`, its test database and, on PostgreSQL, the recorded test pool
  %%> - the users Orbit created for `shop` that no other connection on the server uses
  %%> - system databases such as `mysql` or `postgres` are refused before any run
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether only the record goes, or the database must leave the server
  alt connection without a server
    Note over GW: Delete only the record<br/>R1: no run, database stays
    %%> When:
    %%> - a registered external database or SQLite file, or a Valkey connection that logs in as `default`
    %%> Result:
    %%> - connection `shop` is deleted
    %%> - the database itself stays where it is; Orbit never created it
    %%> - no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Connection destroyed<br/>database kept
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else database on a server
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-database-destroy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
    %%> Inputs:
    %%> - the planned databases, test prefix, test pool and unshared users
    %%> - the vault key name `database-server-3-admin`; the admin password itself never enters the intent
    %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5124
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the task number, at once
    %%> Next:
    %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
    Note over SW: Read the scripts<br/>database-create-command assets
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the shipped destroy phase module and its library on 209, to send them over SSH in argv
    %%> - nothing is copied to Node 12, so nothing is left to clean up
    SW->>N: Drop databases and users<br/>@swamp/ssh · blockers, then drop
    %%> How:
    %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior and the `swamp` role's SSH identity
    %%> - the script reads the admin password from the server's own vault key `database-server-3-admin` on standard input
    %%> What it does, in order:
    %%> - on MySQL, finds the test databases under the recorded test prefix
    %%> - checks the whole set for blockers before the first drop
    %%> - drops each planned database, then each planned user; a missing one counts as removed
    %%> Blocks:
    %%> - PostgreSQL: sessions, replication slots, prepared transactions, subscriptions, outside dependencies of a removed role
    %%> - MySQL: connected clients, metadata locks, outside definers, cross-schema foreign keys
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - any blocker gives `database.in_use`; nothing is dropped
    %%> Per driver:
    %%> - Valkey: no database; `ACL DELUSER` for each user, then `ACL SAVE`; the user's keys stay
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no ownership probe and no connection fence (flow-tighten rule 22); a client that connects between the check and the drop is cut off
    SW->>N: Check they are gone<br/>databases and users absent
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks that no planned database or user is left on the server
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the removal only counts when the server shows it
    Note over SW: Report the result<br/>backend · failed_step · error_code
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - maps the first failed step to its error code, for example `database.in_use`
    Note over SW: Fail on an error<br/>assert · exit code 0
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - fails the run when the report holds an `error_code`, so the task fails with that code
    alt every step passes
      N-->>SW: set absent
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the check passed for every database and user
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
      %%> How the Gateway learns it:
      %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
      Note over GW: Delete the connection<br/>users too · task succeeded
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `shop` and its recorded users are deleted
      %%> - task #5124 succeeds
    else blocked or a drop fails
      N--xSW: in use or exit ≠ 0
      %%> When:
      %%> - a blocker, an ownership refusal, a failed drop, or a lost SSH connection
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
      %%> The Gateway reads:
      %%> - which step failed and its error code, for example `database.in_use`
      Note over GW: Mark the connection failed<br/>task failed · rerun after a fix
      %%> Result:
      %%> - connection `shop` stays, marked failed, with its users and attachments
      %%> - task #5124 fails
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - after a blocker, nothing was dropped
      %%> - after a failed drop, the dropped objects stay gone; there is no rollback
      %%> Retry:
      %%> - stop the clients or remove the blockers, then run the same command again
      %%> - a rerun repeats the checks and counts missing objects as removed
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5124
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
